{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `raw_proportions`, `overshot`, and `distance_tolerance`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added top-level data `raw_proportions` with deterministic relation `raw_proportions[j] = y[j] / n[j]` for each `j`; this replaces the transformed-data observation on the left side of the normal likelihood with a protected top-level data variable. Removed the transformed-data declaration of `raw_proportions`. Split the vectorized prior `[sigma_angle, sigma_distance, sigma_y] ~ normal(0, 1)` into one built-in prior statement per parameter and moved all parameter/protected-data sampling statements before later uses. The likelihood and prior log-density contributions are otherwise unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int J;
  array[J] int n;
  vector[J] x;
  array[J] int y;
  vector[J] raw_proportions;
  real r;
  real R;
  real overshot;
  real distance_tolerance;
}
transformed data {
  vector[J] threshold_angle = asin((R - r) ./ x);
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_angle;
  real<lower=0> sigma_distance;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[J] p_angle;
  vector[J] p_distance;
  vector[J] p;

  sigma_angle ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_distance ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  overshot ~ normal(1, 5);
  distance_tolerance ~ normal(3, 5);

  p_angle = 2 * Phi(threshold_angle / sigma_angle) - 1;
  p_distance = Phi((distance_tolerance - overshot)
                   ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance))
               - Phi((-overshot)
                     ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance));
  p = p_angle .* p_distance;
  raw_proportions ~ normal(p,
                           sqrt(p .* (1 - p) ./ to_vector(n) + sigma_y ^ 2));
}
generated quantities {
  real sigma_degrees = sigma_angle * 180 / pi();
}
